    "https://jobs.uncfsu.edu/postings/29613": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Operations Management",
      "description": "FSU Job Site | Assistant Professor of Operations Management Skip to Main Content Fayetteville State University Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Titles Log In /Create Account Help Applicants FAQ'S Assistant Professor of Operations Management Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. This posting is open until filled, special consideration given to candidates who apply by November 30th. Position Information Position Information Position Title: Assistant Professor of Operations Management Position Number: 002235 Working Title: Assistant Professor of Operations Management Full-time or Part-time: Full Time Time Limited Position: No Number of Vacancies: 1 Department: Management, Marketing, and Entrepreneurship and Fire & Emergency Management Posting Number: 0401432 SHRA/EHRA: EHRA (Faculty) Job Category: Education and Instruction Hiring Range: Commensurate with Education and Experience Overall Position Competency: EHRA Faculty Primary Purpose of the Organization: The Department of Management, Marketing, Entrepreneurship, and FESA ( MMEF ) is dedicated to advancing excellence in business education, research, and community engagement. The department prepares students to become ethical, innovative, and globally competitive leaders by providing high-quality undergraduate and graduate instruction in management, marketing, entrepreneurship, and finance. Through teaching, scholarly activities, experiential learning, and strategic partnerships with industry and community stakeholders, the department develops students’ analytical, leadership, decision-making, and entrepreneurial competencies necessary for success in a dynamic business environment. The department supports the mission of the College of Business and the University by fostering student success, promoting faculty scholarship and professional development, encouraging economic and workforce development, and contributing to the intellectual, social, and economic advancement of the region, state, and global community. Additionally, the department serves as a hub for innovation, business leadership, and applied learning opportunities that enhance career readiness and lifelong learning. Primary Purpose of the Position: The Department of MMEF is seeking highly qualified candidates for a tenure-track, nine-month Assistant Professor position with an expected start date in Fall 2027. The Assistant Professor of Management serves as a faculty member in the Department of Management, Marketing, Entrepreneurship, and FESA ( MMEF ), providing high-quality instruction, scholarly engagement, and service that support the department’s mission and the strategic goals of the College of Business and the University. The position is responsible for teaching undergraduate and graduate courses in management-HR and related business disciplines, maintaining an active program of scholarship, and contributing to student success through advising, mentoring, and experiential learning opportunities. The Assistant Professor of Management is expected to foster a dynamic and inclusive learning environment that prepares students for leadership roles in organizations operating in a global and technology-driven economy. The faculty member contributes to curriculum development and assessment, participates in departmental, college, university, and professional service activities, and engages with business and community stakeholders to enhance academic quality, workforce readiness, and economic development. Through excellence in teaching, research, and service, the position advances the reputation, accreditation standards, and continuous improvement efforts of the MMEF Department and the College of Business. Minimum Education and Experience Requirements: Earned Ph.D. or DBA in Operations Management, Supply Chain Management, Business Analytics, Industrial Engineering, Management Science, or a closely related field from an AACSB -accredited institution (or All but Dissertation ( ABD ) with degree completion prior to appointment). Demonstrated potential for excellence in teaching at the undergraduate and graduate levels. Evidence of research capability and potential for scholarly publication. Strong communication, analytical, and interpersonal skills. Knowledge skills and abilities: A skilled and dedicated teacher with a student-oriented teaching philosophy who is willing to develop real-world and community projects. Preferred Qualifications: Willingness to teach a variety of Management HR courses and other management courses. A record of successful teaching experience. Special Instructions to Applicants: This posting is open until filled, special consideration given to candidates who apply by November 30th. Notice to Applicants: Please make sure that the work history listed on your application is identical to the work history listed on your resume. The application must be filled out completely, Do Not Use the phrase “see resume.” Please list at least three (3) professional references to include a current supervisor. References will only be contact if you are selected for the position and with your permission. Closing Date: Open Until Filled: Yes Additional Information for Applicants: All new employees are required to have listed credentials/degrees verified prior to employment. Transcripts should be provided for all earned degrees and/or the degree which is being used to satisfy credential/qualification requirements. Transcript requests are the responsibility of the candidate. EEO Statement: This position is subject to the successful completion of an employment background check. An employment background check includes a criminal background check, employment verification, reference checks, license verification (if applicable) and credit history check (if applicable). Fayetteville State University is committed to equality of educational opportunity and does not discriminate against applicants, students, or employees based on race, religion, color, national origin, sex, age, disabling condition, political affiliation or sexual orientation. Moreover, Fayetteville State University values diversity and actively seeks to recruit talented students, faculty, and staff from diverse backgrounds. Veteran's Statement: Fayetteville State University is a VEVRAA Federal Contractor and seeks priority referrals of protected veterans for our openings. Quick Link https://jobs.uncfsu.edu/postings/29490 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Optional & Required Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Resume/Curriculum Vitae Unofficial Transcripts (Official Transcripts and Official International Course-by-Course Evaluations Due Upon Hire) Optional Documents Other Document Other Documents Continued Other Documents Continued. MyBronco Portal Bookstore Library Jobs at FSU Contact Us News Events Directory Legal Fayetteville State University 1200 Murchison Road Fayetteville, NC 28301 Copyright © May, 2018 Fayetteville State University. All Rights Reserved. Constituent Institution of The University of North Carolina. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
