    "https://jobs.uncfsu.edu/postings/29570": {
      "title": "2026 -2027 Adjunct Faculty School of Nursing",
      "description": "FSU Job Site | 2026 -2027 Adjunct Faculty School of Nursing Skip to Main Content Fayetteville State University Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Titles Log In /Create Account Help Applicants FAQ'S 2026 -2027 Adjunct Faculty School of Nursing Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. **Applications are purged every 12 months. Applicants are encouraged to reapply if still interested.** Position Information Position Information Position Title: 2026 -2027 Adjunct Faculty School of Nursing Position Number: FA5420 Working Title: Adjunct Lecturer in Nursing Full-time or Part-time: Part Time Time Limited Position: No Number of Vacancies: Multiple Vacancies Department: Temporary Pools Posting Number: 0401434 SHRA/EHRA: EHRA (Faculty) Job Category: Education and Instruction Hiring Range: Commensurate with Education and Experience Overall Position Competency: EHRA Faculty Primary Purpose of the Organization: The School of Nursing at Fayetteville State University is to educate culturally competent, ethical, and caring nurses for a global society. Nursing is a discipline that builds knowledge from nursing theory; the natural, social, and applied sciences; and the humanities. The School of Nursing is committed to educating graduates who will provide evidence-based and patient-centered care. The faculty value the systematic and purposeful application of the nursing process to promote the optimal health of clients throughout the life cycle and in a variety of settings. The School of Nursing strives to produce graduates who appreciate lifelong learning and are contributing to members to the profession of nursing, the community, and society. Primary Purpose of the Position: Fayetteville State University’s School of Nursing is seeking qualified and dedicated candidates for adjunct faculty positions. Adjunct faculty appointments are made on a semester-by-semester basis and may include both online and in-person teaching assignments. The Adjunct Lecturer in Nursing is responsible for delivering high-quality instruction in undergraduate and/or graduate nursing programs. This position supports student learning through classroom, clinical, and/or simulation-based instruction, contributes to curriculum delivery, and engages in service and limited scholarly activities that support the academic mission of the School of Nursing. This posting are continuous in order to develop a qualified pool of interested candidates. If your academic area of interest/expertise meets the programmatic needs of FSU at any time, you will be contacted to discuss proposed opportunities. These needs change from semester to semester. Minimum Education and Experience Requirements: Qualified applicants must have a master’s degree in nursing, with a Bachelor of Science in Nursing. Unencumbered Registered Nursing license in North Carolina or compact state. Two years’ experience in the clinical specialty. Knowledge skills and abilities: Preferred Qualifications: Experience in Clinical Teaching Experience working with online learning management systems to further engage the student learning process. Special Instructions to Applicants: Applications are purged every 12 months. Applicants are encouraged to reapply if still interested. Notice to Applicants: Please make sure that the work history listed on your application is identical to the work history listed on your resume. The application must be filled out completely, Do Not Use the phrase “see resume.” Please list at least three (3) professional references to include a current supervisor. References will only be contact if you are selected for the position and with your permission. Closing Date: Open Until Filled: Yes Additional Information for Applicants: All new employees are required to have listed credentials/degrees verified prior to employment. Transcripts should be provided for all earned degrees and/or the degree which is being used to satisfy credential/qualification requirements. Transcript requests are the responsibility of the candidate. EEO Statement: This position is subject to the successful completion of an employment background check. An employment background check includes a criminal background check, employment verification, reference checks, license verification (if applicable), academic verification and credit history check (if applicable). Fayetteville State University is committed to equality of educational opportunity and employment and does not discriminate against applicants, students, or employees based on race, color, national origin, religion, sex, gender identity, sexual orientation, age, disability, genetic information or veteran status. Moreover, Fayetteville State University values diversity and actively seeks to recruit talented students, faculty, and staff from diverse backgrounds. Veteran's Statement: Fayetteville State University is a VEVRAA Federal Contractor and seeks priority referrals of protected veterans for our openings. Quick Link https://jobs.uncfsu.edu/postings/29569 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a Master's degree? Yes No * Do you have an earned doctoral degree? Yes No * Classes will be offered in both in‑person and online formats. Please indicate which teaching option(s) you are available for. In - Person Online Both Optional & Required Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Resume/Curriculum Vitae Unofficial Transcripts (Official Transcripts and Official International Course-by-Course Evaluations Due Upon Hire) Optional Documents Other Document Other Documents Continued Other Documents Continued. MyBronco Portal Bookstore Library Jobs at FSU Contact Us News Events Directory Legal Fayetteville State University 1200 Murchison Road Fayetteville, NC 28301 Copyright © May, 2018 Fayetteville State University. All Rights Reserved. Constituent Institution of The University of North Carolina. To ensu